<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Flow xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!-- Dead/Pass off-ramp (agent-output/nda-property-and-dead-offramp.md item B). Backs
         quickActions/Opportunity.Mark_Dead.quickAction-meta.xml. See that file's header for the
         full reasoning; the short version: Opportunity.StageName has NO field-level-security grant
         anywhere in this org (confirmed live: zero rows on FieldPermissions for
         Opportunity.StageName), so a plain LDS-backed "Update a Record" quick action would silently
         drop the StageName write for every user. runInMode=SystemModeWithSharing gets the same
         FLS bypass StageAdvanceService's bare `update o;` relies on, while still enforcing sharing
         (this is a user-initiated write, not background automation - it must not let a deal driver
         touch a deal they cannot already see). The Has_Deal_Action_Access decision re-asks the same
         {!$Permission.Acquisition_Deal_Actions} question the FlexiPage visibility rule and
         OpportunityActionPermissionService.assertDealActionAccess() already ask, so the button
         chrome and the flow's own authorization agree by construction. StageName and
         Rejection_Reason__c are written together in ONE Update Records element so
         Rejection_Reason_Required_On_Dead always sees a populated reason - no intermediate save
         that could strand a reason on a live deal. Rejection Reason choices are static (matching
         Opportunity.Rejection_Reason__c's 7 restricted picklist values) rather than a Picklist
         Choice Set - a deliberate, minor drift-risk trade documented here so a future picklist-value
         change is caught by comparing this list against that field, not assumed to stay in sync
         automatically. -->
    <apiVersion>67.0</apiVersion>
